  "findings": [],
  "confirmed_contracts": [
    "Host-only development registry controls source and exact edit paths; final split is rejected.",
    "A pristine source and exact prompt are bound before serializing whole admitted public files; requests over64KiB reject before credentials or child creation.",
    "Fixed HTTPS endpoint, certificate validation, disabled proxies and redirects, exactly one opener POST, no tool definitions, automatic retries or fallback.",
    "Primary credential remains in host memory and Docker stdin; fixed child code alone is mounted, without proposal, home, credential files, scorer or oracle mounts.",
    "Pre-start Docker inspection verifies pinned image, UID, one CPU,2GiB memory/swap,32pids,read-only root,no-new-privileges and dropped capabilities; actual qualified fixture containers were removed.",
    "Duplicate response keys, unauthorized paths, ambiguous replacement strings, invalid structured responses and16KiB patch overflow reject; no returned code is executed by the proposer.",
    "All proposed edits are checked against the complete frozen inventory in a staging tree before application; the separate service must seal and score the resulting exact candidate.",
    "HTTP attempt and usage metadata do not imply settled charges or scientific repair success; absent/lost response remains a possible external effect."
  ],
  "service_integration_requirements": [
    "The reservation.json existence check is not a signature or grant validator. The service must authenticate and durably consume the exact one-use grant, binding registry/unit/request/source/profile/amendment hashes before propose_http.",
    "The service must preserve pending/uncertain reservations and exact transport output; no retry, refund or fresh dispatch inferred from an error.",
    "After proposer cleanup, the service must seal the exact candidate and bind the cold scorer result in its signed public response; live signature/replay/access control is outside this proposer-only review."
  ],
  "qualification_limits": [
    "Ten actual Docker tests used fake credentials, loopback and network=none; no real API/TLS reachability, model response, historical oracle execution or final evaluation is qualified.",
    "Four real development request preflights retained all population members; two fit, two refuse the fixed64KiB whole-file context cap. A changed context policy requires a new consistent profile, not silent truncation.",
    "The180-second limit bounds the attached provider process, while container creation, inspection and cleanup have separate bounded timeouts."
  ],
